  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "decode_R13_R2000",
    "file": "libredwg/src/decode.c",
    "description": "In decode_R13_R2000, the code calls dwg_decode_header_variables(dat, dat, dat, dwg) using the full file Bit_Chain without constraining dat->size/endpoint to the declared header section length (dwg->header_vars.size / section bounds). The generated header parser (header_variables.spec, e.g. FIELD_B at line ~436) repeatedly calls bit_read_B, which reads dat->chain[dat->byte]. Because no effective per-section bound is enforced for these bit reads, malformed header metadata lets parsing run to the end of the fuzz buffer and perform a 1-byte OOB read at bits.c:166.",
    "conditions": "A crafted DWG input must pass initial section checks so decode_R13_R2000 enters Header Variables parsing, then provide inconsistent/forged header variable length/contents so dwg_decode_header_variables continues reading boolean fields past available bytes for that logical section. Data flow: LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput -> dwg_decode -> decode_R13_R2000 -> dwg_decode_header_variables (header_variables.spec FIELD_B sequence) -> bit_read_B, where dat->byte reaches dat->size and reads one byte out of bounds."
  },
